Video2X is a machine learning-based framework for video super resolution
and frame interpolation. It upscales videos, GIFs and images and
increases their frame rate using:

- Anime4K v4 GLSL shaders through FFmpeg's libplacebo filter
- Real-ESRGAN and Real-CUGAN super resolution
- RIFE frame interpolation

The neural networks run on the GPU through ncnn and Vulkan. The port
provides the video2x command line tool, the libvideo2x library and all
bundled models. With the QT6 option it also builds video2x-qt6, the Qt6
interface that queues up files and configures every task separately.
